{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261027-2ae3","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-27T00:00:00Z","claim":"this file was added by the slice but is outside slice A's Footprint. The Footprint at docs/plans/2026-10-27-e18-fix-round-1.md:42 names only result.schema.json, signoff.py, signoff_core/result.py, signoff_core/validate.py and tests/test_fr1_kept_notes.py.","finding":"f1:fa8f5efc58c7403af6fc","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-27-e18-fix-round-1.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/tests/test_fr1_answer_values.py","line":1,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/tests/test_fr1_answer_values.py:1","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"c196aa131247882fa578ff1405ca67bae78dc46cab165d8a2e3522b27c571359","raised_by":"A","scenario":"requirements 4 and 5 were folded into the slice without widening the Footprint. A build-v2 footprint check against line 42 would flag this file, so the slice touched a path its spec does not authorize. test_fr1_kept_notes.py also imports `strict_skill_root` from it, so the authorized test depends on the unauthorized file.","seq":7,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"57f72c58350eaeefe35c619c99bed95206f2b0fd","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261027-2ae3","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-27T00:00:00Z","claim":"requirement 1 still says the note shape is \"the same as `finding` except that `severity` is BLOCKER, MAJOR, MINOR or null\". The built `$defs/note` (result.schema.json:1038) makes location, claim, scenario and evidence_kind string-or-null with no minLength or enum, and makes severity any string. That follows requirement 4 (line 31) and contradicts requirement 1 as written.","finding":"f1:f59c73db50faa3f2bb50","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-27-e18-fix-round-1.md","location":{"file":"docs/plans/2026-10-27-e18-fix-round-1.md","line":28,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"docs/plans/2026-10-27-e18-fix-round-1.md:28","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"16faa449993f5f13becf5485610a9c06e8f385dd737b745a186da306388b1621","raised_by":"A","scenario":"a reader grading against requirement 1 alone sees a note with `severity: \"NOTE\"` and `evidence_kind: \"inferred\"` accepted, which requirement 1 forbids.","seq":8,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"57f72c58350eaeefe35c619c99bed95206f2b0fd","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261027-2ae3","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-27T00:00:00Z","claim":"the schema's top-level description still says it carries the rule that a result with no raised findings has a non-empty `checks_executed`, \"each entry with its output\". This slice removed `output` from the check's `required` and allowed null.","finding":"f1:faa086abc15196e8e445","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-27-e18-fix-round-1.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/references/result.schema.json","line":5,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/references/result.schema.json:5","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"a5ef3a0ff3e6d89e69deaf10171aaceb89950e139fecd64c5e4d58173fcd3e6a","raised_by":"A","scenario":"a consumer trusting the description assumes every recorded check has a string `output`, then reads `null` or a missing key from a valid result.","seq":9,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"57f72c58350eaeefe35c619c99bed95206f2b0fd","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261027-2ae3","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-27T00:00:00Z","claim":"the verdict doc's method lines changed for every check, not only checks with null fields. A check whose output is an empty string used to render \"→ \" and now renders \"→ no output\". A null exit code used to render \"exit None\" and now renders \"no exit code\".","finding":"f1:76720c37f322dc1733dd","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-27-e18-fix-round-1.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff.py","line":1194,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff.py:1194","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"40485a66734498994af8ac032cce2021699a69577fb2739dc0766d1462fefc0a","raised_by":"A","scenario":"a tool or fixture that matches verdict-doc method lines byte for byte sees different text for an empty-output check. I did not run the full suite; `uv run ... -p 'test_*.py'` on the core suite would show whether any fixture depends on it.","seq":10,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"57f72c58350eaeefe35c619c99bed95206f2b0fd","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261027-2ae3","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-27T00:00:00Z","claim":"The pre-write stop now passes `**common` to `finish`, so the raised findings and the notes are in the stopped result. The comment at :855-858 says they \"never make this stop's own result fail\", but that only holds for the result schema. `finish` (signoff.py:197-198, :220-224) also runs `validate.semantic` on the stopped result. The proposal can also be refused by semantic rules that look at those same fields (`/findings` raised outside the source set, `/notes` outside-set note that is in the set). In that case the stop result fails the same rule again, and `finish` exits 4 (EXIT_VALIDATION) instead of 10. The old code dropped findings and notes from this stop, so it could not hit this.","finding":"f1:5919e68b81eb31a9b680","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-27-e18-fix-round-1.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff.py","line":859,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff.py:859","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"230c8be652af85e807a2c7332940c41bae087512bcc540035c9a24e3a1628efd","raised_by":"A","scenario":"`state.json`'s `source_set` and the adjudication's raised/notes partition differ. For example, a run dir edited between `record-answer` and `record`, or a future change to how `in_set` is computed at signoff.py:648-650 versus validate.py:103-105. `record` then refuses the proposal on `/findings`, writes the stopped result, and exits 4 with `semantic` errors. A caller reads that as the station's own validation failure, not a clean stop.","seq":11,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"57f72c58350eaeefe35c619c99bed95206f2b0fd","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261027-2ae3","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-27T00:00:00Z","claim":"The new schema check runs before the `settling` branch, so it also runs on a recovery pass where the receipt already exists. When it refuses there, the stop reports `writes_none: true` and `answer_refused: true`, even though the receipt may show project writes that already landed (log appends, block, card). The stop does not use `partial_from_receipt`, so the record says nothing was written when something was.","finding":"f1:201c09c530759fe0f49d","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-27-e18-fix-round-1.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff.py","line":847,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff.py:847","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"53fe37fe7983b4cf2cb31c39e4c0cdf05dcf076b67bd295ca1f92b1012f6dce7","raised_by":"A","scenario":"An old-version run (the live run's shape) lands the verdict doc, the records and the card, then dies or exits before it commits. Recovery `record` then runs under a schema that refuses the proposal. The result claims `writes_none` while the log holds this run's events. The semantic-only check had the same exposure before; this slice widens what can refuse there.","seq":12,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"57f72c58350eaeefe35c619c99bed95206f2b0fd","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
